│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_microstructure_volatility_signal                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses static thresholds (0.2% for entry, 0.4% TP, 0.3% SL) regardless  │
│                          │ of market conditions, which limits adaptability. Key improvements:                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Adaptive Entry Thresholds**: Instead of fixed 0.2% threshold, scale entry            │
│                          │ requirements based on realized volatility (vol_20) and order book imbalance (obi_tau5).   │
│                          │ High volatility requires stronger signals; strong OBI confirms conviction.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Volatility-Adjusted Risk Management**: TP and SL are now functions of ATR and        │
│                          │ current volatility regime, not fixed percentages. This prevents over-aggressive exits in  │
│                          │ calm markets and under-aggressive exits in volatile ones.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Microstructure Confirmation Filters**: Add order book pressure (book_pressure_3,     │
│                          │ kyle_lambda_est, depth_ratio_5) and spread conditions to filter false signals. Only trade │
│                          │ when microstructure supports the predicted direction.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Session and Funding Rate Awareness**: Reduce position size during low-liquidity      │
│                          │ sessions (Asia) and near funding events. Increase size during high-conviction US session  │
│                          │ with favorable funding.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Asymmetric Position Sizing**: Long trades get larger positions when trend_strength   │
│                          │ is high and price is above VWAP; shorts get larger positions when momentum is negative    │
│                          │ and price is below VWAP.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 6. **Dynamic Max Bars**: Extend holding period in strong trends (trend_strength > 0.6) to │
│                          │ capture larger moves; reduce in choppy markets (autocorr_5 < 0.2).                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes leverage the rich bar_context to adapt to market microstructure, volatility │
│                          │ regimes, and session dynamics, improving Sharpe ratio through better risk-adjusted        │
│                          │ returns and win rate through better entry confirmation.                                   │
