│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the fixed-threshold, fixed-size logic with a context-aware asymmetric  │
│                          │ signal engine. It uses predicted_return as the base edge, then tightens or loosens entry  │
│                          │ criteria using microstructure quality (spread, OBI, book pressure, Kyle lambda),          │
│                          │ volatility regime (ATR, vol ratios, bb_pct), trend confirmation, funding pressure, and    │
│                          │ session timing. Position size is scaled by edge quality and penalized in noisy/high-cost  │
│                          │ regimes. Take-profit, stop-loss, and max_bars are adapted to volatility and expected      │
│                          │ regime persistence. This should improve Sharpe and Calmar by reducing trades in adverse   │
│                          │ conditions while keeping larger exposure when multiple signals align.                     │
