│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ensemble_regime_adaptive_signal                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This algorithm takes a fundamentally different approach by implementing an ensemble-based │
│                          │ regime detection system combined with adaptive thresholds. Instead of using fixed or      │
│                          │ linearly-adjusted thresholds, it:                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Regime Classification**: Classifies market conditions into 4 distinct regimes        │
│                          │ (Trending-High-Vol, Mean-Revert-Low-Vol, Choppy-High-Vol, Quiet-Low-Vol) using a          │
│                          │ combination of trend strength, volatility ratios, autocorrelation, and skew/kurtosis.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Regime-Specific Logic**: Each regime has its own entry thresholds, position sizing   │
│                          │ rules, and exit parameters. This allows the algorithm to be aggressive in favorable       │
│                          │ regimes and defensive in unfavorable ones.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Multi-Factor Confirmation**: Uses a weighted ensemble of microstructure (OBI,        │
│                          │ spread, depth), momentum (returns, RSI, MACD), and macro (funding) signals rather than    │
│                          │ simple threshold crossing.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Dynamic Risk Management**: Position sizing and stops adapt not just to volatility,   │
│                          │ but to regime-specific risk profiles. Mean-revert regimes get tighter stops; trending     │
│                          │ regimes get wider stops.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Liquidity-Aware Entry**: Combines spread, depth ratio, and kyle_lambda into a        │
│                          │ liquidity score that gates entries and scales position size.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 6. **Session-Aware Micro Adjustments**: Uses time-of-day signals (hour_sin/cos) to        │
│                          │ fine-tune thresholds within sessions, not just binary session flags.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should perform better:                                                           │
│                          │ - The prior best performer (80.50 score) used extreme simplicity with high selectivity    │
│                          │ (462 trades, 78% win rate). This approach maintains that selectivity while adding         │
│                          │ intelligent regime adaptation.                                                            │
│                          │ - The complex weighted approach (11.63 score) suffered from over-parameterization and     │
│                          │ conflicting signals. This ensemble approach is more modular and interpretable.            │
│                          │ - By classifying regimes first, we avoid applying the same logic to fundamentally         │
│                          │ different market conditions, which is a key source of drawdown.                           │
│                          │ - The multi-factor confirmation reduces false signals while the regime-specific           │
│                          │ thresholds increase true signal capture in favorable conditions.                          │
