│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_ensemble_gate                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This design borrows the broad ideas from the earlier programs — threshold-based entry,    │
│                          │ microstructure confirmation, and volatility-aware exits — but changes the internal logic  │
│                          │ from a simple filter stack into a compact regime ensemble.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Instead of using one or two hard gates, the new algorithm builds a directional “edge      │
│                          │ score” from several orthogonal components:                                                │
│                          │ - model prediction strength,                                                              │
│                          │ - order-book pressure and depth alignment,                                                │
│                          │ - trend and momentum quality,                                                             │
│                          │ - mean-reversion risk via RSI, Bollinger position, wick rejection, and VWAP distance,     │
│                          │ - market quality via spread, Kyle lambda, and funding timing.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key novelty is that these factors are fused into a signed confidence score that       │
│                          │ determines not just whether to trade, but how asymmetric the risk should be. Strong       │
│                          │ trend-confirmation regimes receive wider take-profit than stop-loss, while stretched or   │
│                          │ unstable regimes get tighter stops and smaller size. Position sizing is also conditioned  │
│                          │ on a separate liquidity-friction penalty, so the strategy scales down in noisy or         │
│                          │ expensive-to-trade environments rather than just rejecting them.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this is a regime-scored, asymmetry-driven decision engine rather than a          │
│                          │ fixed-rule signal filter, which should better adapt to the rich context without looking   │
│                          │ ahead.                                                                                    │
