│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the high-performing dynamic volatility thresholding and           │
│                          │ microstructure filters from the 87.56-score program with enhanced position sizing and     │
│                          │ slight refinement of trade entry quality metrics.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1.  **Dynamic Thresholding:** Uses the successful volatility-regime-based thresholding    │
│                          │ logic (`0.0018 * (0.9 + 0.2 * vol_regime)`), which adapts to expanding or contracting     │
│                          │ volatility to manage trade frequency.                                                     │
│                          │ 2.  **Proven Microstructure Quality:** Inherits the weighted Microstructure Quality index │
│                          │ (OBI 1, 3, 5 + Book Pressure) that resulted in a win rate of 0.78.                        │
│                          │ 3.  **Enhanced Position Sizing:** Increases the base position size slightly (from 0.12 to │
│                          │ 0.13) and incorporates conviction-based scaling (boosting size to 0.15 for high predicted │
│                          │ returns) and session session-based boosts (favoring the volatility of the US session).    │
│                          │ 4.  **Preserved Exit Logic:** Maintains the extremely robust 0.004/0.003                  │
│                          │ Take-Profit/Stop-Loss ratio which has repeatedly produced high Calmar and Sharpe ratios   │
│                          │ in previous iterations.                                                                   │
│                          │ 5.  **Strict Cost & Funding Filters:** Filters out trades during high spread or extreme   │
│                          │ funding regimes to prevent slippage and carry-cost erosion.                               │
