│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Adds stronger entry filters using order-book imbalance, depth, spread, kyle lambda,     │
│                          │ RSI, MACD, VWAP deviation, Bollinger position, trend strength, autocorrelation, and       │
│                          │ funding.                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Separates momentum-trend entries from mean-reversion entries so the model can exploit   │
│                          │ both continuation and reversion regimes without lookahead.                                │
│                          │ - Makes thresholds adaptive to volatility and execution cost, reducing low-quality trades │
│                          │ when spreads or impact are elevated.                                                      │
│                          │ - Uses volatility-adjusted asymmetric exits: long and short trades get different TP/SL    │
│                          │ multipliers based on regime quality and trend confirmation.                               │
│                          │ - Scales position size by conviction and liquidity quality instead of a flat size, while  │
│                          │ keeping bounds conservative to protect win rate and drawdown.                             │
│                          │ - Tightens time-in-trade in noisy or cost-heavy regimes and allows a little more runway   │
│                          │ when trend and book quality align.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to improve combined score by preserving the current high win rate while       │
│                          │ increasing average trade quality, especially in toxic-flow or choppy conditions.          │
