│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ contextual_asymmetry_filter                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This edit upgrades the current fixed-threshold approach into a context-aware, asymmetric  │
│                          │ entry engine that uses the richer feature set already available in `bar_context`.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main improvements:                                                                        │
│                          │ - Adds microstructure confirmation from multiple OBI horizons, spread, depth, book        │
│                          │ pressure, and Kyle lambda.                                                                │
│                          │ - Uses price-action regime features to distinguish trend continuation from                │
│                          │ exhaustion/mean reversion.                                                                │
│                          │ - Introduces volatility-adjusted thresholds so the model is more selective during noisy   │
│                          │ regimes and more responsive during stable ones.                                           │
│                          │ - Adds funding/session guards to avoid low-quality trades around carry pressure and       │
│                          │ illiquid periods.                                                                         │
│                          │ - Uses asymmetric long/short sizing based on signal quality instead of a flat fixed size. │
│                          │ - Adapts take-profit, stop-loss, and max-hold time to volatility and regime, with tighter │
│                          │ risk in choppy conditions and slightly wider targets when flow and trend agree.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to improve win rate and profit factor while preserving enough trade frequency │
│                          │ to avoid over-filtering.                                                                  │
