│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ micro_regime_adaptive_sizing                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The proposed strategy improves upon the previous seed by implementing a more              │
│                          │ sophisticated volatility-adaptive thresholding mechanism and a multi-factor               │
│                          │ microstructure filter.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1.  **Volatility-Regime Thresholding**: Instead of static thresholds, the entry           │
│                          │ requirement scales with the ratio of short-term (5-bar) to medium-term (20-bar)           │
│                          │ volatility. This prevents over-trading during low-volatility noise and ensures the        │
│                          │ predicted return is significant relative to current market conditions.                    │
│                          │ 2.  **Microstructure Confirmation**: Uses a weighted composite of Order Book Imbalance    │
│                          │ (OBI) across multiple time horizons (tau 1, 3, 5) and book pressure to confirm the        │
│                          │ XGBoost model's direction. This filters out signals that lack liquidity support.          │
│                          │ 3.  **Asymmetric Risk & Sizing**:                                                         │
│                          │     *   Increases position size during the US session and when the model shows high       │
│                          │ conviction (abs return > 0.35%).                                                          │
│                          │     *   Uses a slightly tighter stop-loss (0.0028) relative to the take-profit (0.004) to │
│                          │ improve the Sharpe ratio and Profit Factor, while maintaining a high win rate.            │
│                          │ 4.  **Macro & Execution Filters**: Filters entries based on the funding rate (carry cost) │
│                          │ and spread (execution cost). It also adds a VWAP deviation check to avoid entering at     │
│                          │ local price extremes.                                                                     │
