│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_asymmetric_filters                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This edit upgrades the signal logic from a fixed-threshold seed into a regime-aware,      │
│                          │ asymmetric entry system that uses the richer bar context already available.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Entry thresholds are dynamically widened or tightened using spread, Kyle lambda,        │
│                          │ volatility, funding pressure, and session regime.                                         │
│                          │ - Long/short entries are no longer symmetric: longs favor positive order-book imbalance,  │
│                          │ positive trend, supportive VWAP/RSI; shorts favor the inverse.                            │
│                          │ - Price rejection filters use wick ratios, Bollinger position, and VWAP deviation to      │
│                          │ avoid chasing extended moves.                                                             │
│                          │ - Position size is scaled by confidence and discounted in toxic-liquidity or              │
│                          │ high-volatility conditions.                                                               │
│                          │ - Take-profit and stop-loss are volatility-adjusted using ATR, with tighter exits in      │
│                          │ mean-reverting or funding-stressed regimes and wider targets in trending regimes.         │
│                          │ - Hold time adapts to trend persistence, autocorrelation, and session type, improving the │
│                          │ tradeoff between win rate and expectancy.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve combined score by preserving the current decent trade frequency while │
│                          │ reducing low-quality entries and making risk placement more regime-sensitive.             │
