│                          │ 1. **Asymmetric Microstructure Filtering**: Enhanced signal entry filters that check for  │
│                          │ depth imbalance (depth_ratio) and directional book pressure alignment. When the order     │
│                          │ book shows structural weakness (low depth ratio or reversed pressure), we reduce or       │
│                          │ reject signals despite favorable price prediction. This catches false breakouts in thin   │
│                          │ markets.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **ATR-Anchored Dynamic Stops**: Rather than using only vol_impulse (ratio of           │
│                          │ volatilities), we incorporate actual bar volatility (ATR) into stop-loss calculation. ATR │
│                          │ captures realized volatility of recent bars and provides a more immediate risk adjustment │
│                          │ than volatility ratios. This should tighten drawdowns while maintaining entry quality.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **RSI Extremes Conviction Dampening**: When predicted_return is positive but RSI_14 is │
│                          │ already extremely elevated (>75), or predicted_return is negative but RSI_14 is already   │
│                          │ extremely depressed (<25), we reduce signal conviction by 20%. This filters               │
│                          │ mean-reversion traps that occur when price momentum reverses from extremes, improving win │
│                          │ rate in ranging markets.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These three changes work synergistically:                                                 │
│                          │ - Microstructure filtering improves entry quality (higher % of true breakouts)            │
│                          │ - ATR stops adapt to realized bar volatility (tighter risk management)                    │
│                          │ - RSI dampening reduces false signals in mean-reversion prone conditions (better          │
│                          │ Calmar/win-rate)                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Combined effect: Fewer but higher-quality trades with better risk-reward, improved profit │
│                          │ factor and Calmar ratio.                                                                  │
