│ patch_description        │ The current program generates 535 trades with a profit factor of 15.13, slightly          │
│                          │ underperforming Seed 2/3 at 530 trades with 15.95. The issue is likely that while the     │
│                          │ elastic threshold mechanism works well, it lacks confirmation filters on actual price     │
│                          │ action.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This mutation adds RSI and Bollinger Band filters to entry logic:                         │
│                          │ - For LONG signals: require RSI < 70 (not overbought) AND BB% < 0.8 (room to run up)      │
│                          │ - For SHORT signals: require RSI > 30 (not oversold) AND BB% > 0.2 (room to run down)     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These are lightweight confirmations that filter out low-quality reversals and exhaustion  │
│                          │ patterns, reducing false signals without requiring additional microstructure data. The    │
│                          │ bounds are conservative (0.2-0.8 vs 0.0-1.0) to avoid over-filtering during strong        │
│                          │ trends.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should reduce trade count toward 530 while improving win rate and profit factor by   │
│                          │ eliminating marginal entries that lack price action confirmation.                         │
