│ patch_description        │ This edit upgrades the signal logic from a single-threshold liquidity filter into a       │
│                          │ regime-aware, asymmetric entry engine. It uses richer context already available in the    │
│                          │ bar data: short/medium order-book imbalance, volatility state, RSI extremes, Bollinger    │
│                          │ position, VWAP deviation, funding pressure, minutes-to-funding, and session flags.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The idea is to improve the combined score by:                                             │
│                          │ - being more selective in low-quality conditions,                                         │
│                          │ - allowing larger/earlier long entries when momentum and microstructure align,            │
│                          │ - requiring stronger confirmation for shorts during squeezes or bullish funding regimes,  │
│                          │ - sizing positions with confidence and volatility adjustment,                             │
│                          │ - widening or tightening TP/SL dynamically based on regime strength,                      │
│                          │ - extending hold time only when trend persistence supports it.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the implementation fully self-contained and avoids lookahead or external       │
│                          │ dependencies.                                                                             │
