│                          │ - asymmetric long/short behavior, since longs and shorts often behave differently around  │
│                          │ funding and session liquidity;                                                            │
│                          │ - volatility-adjusted exits that widen slightly in strong trends and tighten when the     │
│                          │ market is noisy but not directional.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to reduce low-quality trades while preserving the profitable edge in strong   │
